On-device AI refers to a type of AI where the algorithms are trained and executed directly on a device, not the cloud. It means the AI doesn't require internet connectivity to function. For example, when you use a smartphone, the AI might analyze images or text in real-time on your device itself, not relying on cloud services. This approach allows for quicker responses and privacy features without needing external data.

